    "objectID": "index.html",
    "href": "index.html",
    "title": "An introduction to Pynapple",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Welcome to this introduction to Pynapple.\nPynapple is a python package for analysing neural data.\nThe package is actively maintained by the Flatiron Institute’s neuroRSE team.\nThe only thing you’ll need to follow along is a working Python environment with pynapple installed:\npip install pynapple\nNow just open your favourite way of running Python, and follow along!",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Preface</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "origins.html",
    "href": "origins.html",
    "title": "2  Origins",
    "section": "",
    "text": "2000: TSToolbox, MATLAB\nMcNaughton lab: David Redish & Francesco Battaglia\n2016: TSToolbox2, MATLAB\nAdrien Peyrache & Luke Sjulson\n2018: neuroseries, Python\nFrancesco Battaglia\n2021: pynapple, Python\nGuillaume Viejo\n\n\npresently with the Flatiron Institute’s neuroRSE team:\n\nGuillaume Viejo\nSarah Jo Venditto\nEdoardo Balzani\nWilliam Broderick\n\n+ me, a 2025 neuroRSE intern",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>2</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Origins</span>"
    ]
